Subject: CPMS I03A Host Admission Evidence Protocol Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 2fd52931-7385-44ae-804e-86491dabc734
@ [canonical_specification_uuid] 906cbed0-8140-437c-b96b-f6b03535f26a

& [Problem] the prior release denial was preserved correctly but its source events later rolled out of a small circular Code Integrity log
  + delayed absence can be misread as no denial
  + an aggregate PowerShell invocation previously allowed a later metadata query to hide the build subcommand exit
  + reused target output could obscure whether a required helper actually participated

& [Decision] define one-command fresh-target attempts with immediate pre and post channel capture
  + seal raw selected XML normalized projections streams result and artifact states before rollover
  + classify channel discontinuity wrapper faults truncation and missing evidence as incomplete
  + require a conjunctive admission result

& [WhyNotRetryNow] I03A has no active implementation signature exact four-surface diff or admitted dependency lock
  + the current workstation already produced user-visible policy blocks
  + more retries would add notifications without closing authority prerequisites

& [WhyNotTreatNoCurrentEventAsPass] the log oldest retained time is later than the preserved denial
  + circular retention explains the missing historical record
  + only a bounded continuous future attempt can use event silence as subordinate evidence

& [WhyFreshTarget] cached success can avoid the helper whose launch policy is being tested
  + a new empty target makes compilation and test participation attributable
  + locked source cache remains a separately identified non-output input

& [WhyAllowlistEnvironment] reproducibility needs selected toolchain and build state while full environment capture risks credentials and irrelevant personal data
& [Cost] greater evidence volume and slower separately captured gates
& [Benefit] a blocked pass failed or incomplete decision can be reconstructed without UI memory or shell-state ambiguity
& [AuthorityLimit] justification supports protocol formation only and no retry or policy action
& [Disposition] is justified_for_protocol_formation
